__label__bookssiddhartha about the author nobel prize winner hermann hesse was born in calw in the black forest germany in 1877 his parents were both missionaries his first novel peter camenzind 1904 was a success but world war i brought him into conflict with rampant german nationalism in 1923 he traded in his german citizenship for a swiss passport his most famous books include siddhartha steppenwolf narziss und goldmund and the glass bead game
